From aa59e723b4845fa8992ef7eeb66d8f005dd7c2bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hans Bihs <hans.bihs@ntnu.no>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:33:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Checkpoints: REEF3D::CORAL and multi-block grids

REEF3D::CORAL (Z 40) runs are now checkpointable (P 48, I 45, G 46) with
CFD, NHFLOW and FNPF:
- coral_state.h: the state of a run as a vector of doubles
- save_state/load_state for the model, the integrator (Jacobian
  refactorized), every load with history (hydro, fluid loads, fluid
  members, moorings, PTO elements and controllers), the sampled
  kinematics and the body tracks; coupling and coral_reef3d on top
- the blob "coral" in the checkpoint; set after the set-up in coral_ini;
  the restart skips static equilibrium, modes and first output and
  continues the time series and the journal
- NHFLOW external dynamics: no initial loads on a restart
- FSI (Z 10) and FEM (Z 30) stay refused

Multi-block grids (geo_mb > 0) for NHFLOW and SFLOW: the blocks 1.. are
level-0 patches in the AMR checkpoint (reefamr_ckpt), NHFLOW SI face
discharges of the blocks restored; the refusals are removed.

Output continuity: the NHFLOW and SFLOW SI logs continue on a restart,
the SFLOW initial debug dump only on a fresh start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WSsBQ8fXSWupNenPc2yAMJ
